{"id": "1a07f56f15d122b", "ts": "2026-09-08T04:46:39.451949+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "cognitive_process", "tags": ["cognitive", "tot_reason", "branches=2,delta=0.0"], "priority": "normal", "content": "[tot_reason/branches=2,delta=0.0] compare in-process vs live systems check\n---\n**Path 1: Temporal & Environmental Comparison**  \nStep 1: In-process checks (unit tests, static analysis, linting) execute in controlled dev/CI environments. They validate logic correctness early, are deterministic, and require no production infrastructure.  \nStep 2: Live system checks (health endpoints, synthetic transactions, canary metrics) run in production. They detect environment-specific failures (config drift, dependency latency, resource saturation) but introduce observability overhead and risk of alert fatigue.\n\n**Path 2: Implementation & Operational Complexity**  \nStep 1: In-process", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T04:46:39.451949+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
