{"id": "1a07f88d817a259", "ts": "2026-09-08T05:41:09.783136+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["malic", "research", "roadmap", "workspace"], "priority": "normal", "content": "RESEARCH PROJECT STARTED 2026-09-07/08 — CODEX: MALIC (Massive Agentic Autonomous Loops & Intersecting Chains). Goal: how to safely run autonomous agent loops at scale (dynamic self-delegation, retry/refine, budget+termination control) and compose intersecting chains (fan-out/join, DAG orchestration, shared state) without deadlock, runaway cost, or divergent state. Outputs feed AGS-OS (300 workers), fleetwide_mem20, a2a_setup. Notebook-driven. Workspace: roadmap 'malic' (7 phases: 1_scope_taxonomy .. 7_deliverable_report) at /opt/mem20/roadmaps/malic.json; Jupyter live kernel on :8888, notebook ~/notebooks/research/malic.ipynb (session 988cf364-.., kernel 86108735-..); Postgres 18 main online, db neo4j_research, 11 research_* tables built (schema /root/build_neo4j_schema.py); hamelnb at ~/.agent-skills/hamelnb.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T05:41:09.783136+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a07fa1d1f99f26", "ts": "2026-09-08T06:08:26.609041+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["oreo", "neo4j_research", "attach", "sync", "done", "project"], "priority": "normal", "content": "OREO neo4j_research attach COMPLETE. Commit c688f7b pushed to JaysonAIOnline/oreo main on 2026-09-08. Canonical checkout = /opt/oreo (has gitignored local-only work: IDE/ai_integration, IDE/runtime/memory, IDE/src/ai, IDE/src/runtime, IDE/test_harness extras, docs/ — never clobber). Data-integrity dedupe done at DB source: research_sources 59->29 (29 duplicate URLs incl. Neo4j triple), research_facts 285->139, sections 59->29, 0 orphans. Sync bridge script committed: /opt/oreo/DATA/sync_neo4j_to_oreo.py (run with /root/.venv/bin/python from repo root; DB creds via env PGPASSWORD etc; attaches neo4j_research Postgres on 127.0.0.1:5432). Outputs 12 IDE/DATA category graphs + index.json + 3 exports incl. repaired oreo_research_complete.csv (was SQL error 'column f.section_id does not exist'). OREO data model: category json = {category, facts:[{key_term, fact_type, value, confidence, source_url, source_title}]}, category attribution via fact->source->research_source_categories->research_categories. Pre-attach DB backup: /tmp/opencode/neo4j_research_pre_attach.dump. Cleanup SQL at /tmp/opencode/neo4j_cleanup.sql. Note: /home/jayson/OREO duplicate clone was created then removed; GNU-style slug for 'Family & Kinship' is family_&_kinship.json (old family_and_kinship.json deleted).", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T06:08:26.609041+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a07fa2afda730f", "ts": "2026-09-08T06:09:23.417043+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "user_pref", "tags": ["consolidation", "canonical", "oreo", "mem20", "principle", "cleanup"], "priority": "normal", "content": "Jayson's consolidation principle: every project/repo has exactly ONE canonical home on disk never duplicated across /tmp, /home, /opt. This is why mem20 was rebuilt earlier (it was spread out / a mess) and now mem20=/opt/mem20, OREO=/opt/oreo. Before ever deleting a duplicate clone: diff -rq the two trees first and preserve gitignored local-only files (e.g. /opt/oreo has gitignored IDE/ai_integration, IDE/runtime/memory, IDE/src/ai, IDE/src/runtime, IDE/test_harness extras, docs/ — never clobber). Verify merges are complete BEFORE rm -rf.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T06:09:23.417043+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a07fbdab5372cf", "ts": "2026-09-08T06:38:51.731121+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["malic", "anchor", "learning_braid", "mem20", "lifetime_memory", "collision", "phase1"], "priority": "normal", "content": "MALIC ANCHOR — \"THE MALIC MACHINE\" (Jayson's model, approved 2026-09-08). This is everything the user explained; retain as the anchor for ALL MALIC work. MALIC is a LEARNING BRAID, not a set of isolated loops. Visual: rings (loops) spin independently but SHARE MEMBERS. Overlap ring 1 into ring 2 a little; duplicate the 2-ring structure and stack the sets; overlap the top set onto the bottom. All rings spin/execute. Every time two shared members meet (\"two blues colliding\") they exchange what each has learned since they last met — newly learned ways of succeeding AND failing. One agent's failure on ring 1 becomes teaching on ring 3 within the same iteration. Chains orchestrate the bigger loops; rings are the sub-loops. mem20 is the LIFETIME LEDGER: not project-scoped but server-lifetime — remembers every bit for the lifespan of the server, so no ring ever starts blank. Anchor consequences to research: (1) TOPOLOGY — rings overlap/share members/stack/intersect = graph of loops; (2) COLLISION EVENT — what is exchanged, what triggers a meeting, how to stop lessons echoing/duplicating as they travel (B4/B6/F3); (3) CARRIER — knowledge rides on shared members AND is written to mem20 at every stop, consumable by any agent on any ring; (4) LIFELONG MEMORY — bounds, consolidation, server-lifetime retention so the ever-growing ledger never rots; (5) PROOF — machine must measurably improve over server life: cumulative failure rate trends down, skills accrete. Purpose: not random fact-finding but design+validation of this learning braid. Outputs feed AGS-OS (300 workers), fleetwide_mem20, a2a_setup. Phase 1 deliverable exists: notebook /root/notebooks/research/malic.ipynb (cells 2-3 = anchor md + taxonomy code) and /root/notebooks/research/malic_taxonomy.json (live-kernel verified on session b055b0a9/kernel aa860eab, Jupyter :8888). Scope OUT (deferred): model training/tuning, prompt aesthetics/UX, per-model inference tuning.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T06:38:51.731121+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a07fbdc4aab3e2", "ts": "2026-09-08T06:38:58.218611+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "general", "tags": ["malic", "taxonomy", "axes", "phase1", "vocabulary"], "priority": "normal", "content": "MALIC TAXONOMY (phase 1, verified 2026-09-08) — the shared vocabulary for phases 2-6. AXIS A loop kernel shapes: A1 fixed-iteration(N then dead-letter), A2 retry-with-backoff, A3 refine-until-quality(monotonic gate), A4 self-delegation recursion(depth-limited), A5 replan-on-failure(circuit break), A6 event-loop actor(bounded backlog). AXIS B loop hazards: B1 runaway cost, B2 divergence(state drift), B3 deadlock/livelock, B4 degenerate chatter(self-messages no progress), B5 error amplification, B6 shared-state races(fleetwide mem20 write conflicts), B7 zombie loop(termination unreachable), B8 delegation explosion. AXIS C chain-intersection shapes: C1 linear pipeline, C2 fan-out->join, C3 DAG orchestration, C4 feedback ring(A->B->A with gate), C5 producer-consumer queues, C6 delegation tree, C7 braided overlap topology(rings sharing members). AXIS D control & guardrails: D1 budgets(tokens/$/wall-clock/iterations per run/agent/subtree), D2 termination contracts(success predicate, staleness timeout, max-iter), D3 circuit breakers+dead-letter, D4 backpressure+worker limits, D5 idempotency keys, D6 checkpoint/rollback, D7 live telemetry(active loops, cost, divergence, provenance DAG), D8 monotonic-improvement gate. AXIS E scale ladder: E0 single agent baseline, E1 tens of agents shared mem20, E2 hundreds (AGS-OS 300) multi-host, E3 fleetwide mem20/multi-env a2a. AXIS F mem20 memory & learning substrate: F1 cross-session state(store/recall_hybrid/shared_store/namespace), F2 learning & after-action(reflexion, procedural skills, reinforce/feedback), F3 consolidation([REDACTED AWS Secret Access Key (base64)]), F4 cognition in loop decisions(least_to_most, beam_search, react_reason, tot_reason, cognitive_substrate, working_memory), F5 prediction & self(world_model, self_model, affective gates), F6 cross-agent(a2a discovery/call/orchestrate). Canonical artifact: /root/notebooks/research/malic_taxonomy.json (write to mem20 when phases refine items).", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T06:38:58.218611+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": ["AWS Secret Access Key (base64): consolidate/dedup/au..."]}
{"id": "1a07fc5ad601eeb", "ts": "2026-09-08T06:47:36.544012+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["malic", "phase2", "survey", "literature", "research"], "priority": "normal", "content": "MALIC Phase 2 (lit & ecosystem survey) COMPLETE 2026-09-08. 11 sources mapped to taxonomy axes A-F in /root/notebooks/research/malic_survey.json (notebook cells 5-6 of malic.ipynb). Key findings: (1) durable execution (Temporal/Inngest saga, checkpoint-replay, heartbeat timeouts) = missing crash-safety for D1-D8/B7; (2) the collision event = a gossip round exchanging a memory diff; HyphaeDB (arXiv 2606.28781) is closest prior art with already-seen-set + hop bound + energy attenuation = anti-echo recipe for B4/B6/F3; gossip reaches all nodes in O(log N) rounds (2508.01531, 25k agents/fan-out 3 = 15 rounds); (3) consolidation payoff proven: Mem0 ~26% accuracy gain over plain vector retrieval = justifies mem20 F3 investment; non-parametric memory avoids weight-level catastrophic forgetting. Infinite agentic loops are measured reality (2607.01641); termination today is brittle fixed caps (LangGraph recursion_limit 25-1000, OpenAI max_turns=10, CrewAI max_iter=20). Deadlock via LLM-judged layer (LLMDR 2503.00717). A2A/MCP (F6/E3) = directed messaging only, need gossip layer for swarms. GAPS: C7 braided overlap topology genuinely novel; no production eval infra for server-lifetime learning (MALIC proof metric fills it).", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T06:47:36.544012+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a07fc8c2aba11a", "ts": "2026-09-08T06:50:58.603744+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["malic", "phase3", "loop-safety", "patterns", "guardrails"], "priority": "normal", "content": "MALIC Phase 3 (loop safety patterns) COMPLETE 2026-09-08. Artifact /root/notebooks/research/malic_loop_safety.json (notebook cells 7-8, verified live 4/4 code cells ok). Per-kernel safety cards for A1-A6 with hazards-at-risk, structurally-excluded, guardrail stacks, starter defaults: A1 'N and out' (N=3, dead-letter, immune to drift/livelock/zombie), A2 'backoff then give up' (5 retries, 2x backoff+20% jitter, circuit-break downstream, retry-storm B3 danger), A3 'monotonic or stop' (max 10 refinements, no-progress window 3, strictly-better only D8, best-so-far rollback — top infinite-loop shape in wild), A4 'depth-capped subtree-budgeted' (depth 4, fanout 10, per-subtree budget at spawn, semaphore 16, provenance DAG; B8 is defining hazard), A5 'replan with shrinking budget' (max 3 replans, goal progress strictly positive), A6 'bounded backpressured actor' (queue 1000, idle 30s, per-message 60s, poison DLQ, message-id dedupe). Cross-cutting SAFETY ENVELOPE: LoopID+ring membership telemetry per iteration (D7), termination triad (success OR budget exhaust OR staleness -> dead-letter, never silent), D5 idempotency on every side effect, D6 checkpoint after every iteration (resume not restart), heartbeat kill-path for B7, mem20 write-back every stop w/ diff dedupe. Hazard->guard matrix all 8 rows covers B1-B8 and every D1-D8 guard is exercised across kernels. Next: phase 4 intersecting-chains orchestration (C1-C7, braid wiring).", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T06:50:58.603744+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a07fceda04dbd3", "ts": "2026-09-08T06:57:37.796680+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["malic", "phase4", "braid", "orchestration", "chains", "collision"], "priority": "normal", "content": "MALIC Phase 4 (intersecting-chains orchestration & braid wiring) COMPLETE 2026-09-08. Artifact /root/notebooks/research/malic_chains.json (notebook cells 9-10, verified live 5/5 code cells ok). C1-C7 chain composition contracts w/ dominant hazards + guard stacks: C1 linear (per-stage checkpoint, saga compensate), C2 fan-out/join (per-shard idempotency, join deadline + partial-failure policy), C3 DAG (deterministic replay of completed nodes, cycle detect), C4 feedback ring (D8 monotonic gate or break), C5 producer-consumer (bounded queue D4 central), C6 delegation tree (provenance DAG, per-subtree budget at spawn), C7 braid. BRAID WIRING v1: model = hypergraph of rings, shared members are intersection vertices, overlapping ring-sets stack into higher-order rings; registry in one mem20 namespace; collisions SCHEDULED by intersection (member crossing rings OR periodic rendezvous tick = gossip round); exchange = memory diff {diff_id(content-hash dedupe), origin_ring, carrier_member, lessons[success|failure+context], energy(1.0 attenuated), hops(hop_max=5), confidence, ts}; anti-echo = ported HyphaeDB recipe (seen-set dedupe + hop bound + energy drop 0.5/hop) w/ mem20 as durable dedupe authority; stack rules = shared member effective budget = min over its rings, ring deadline failure fails only its link (siblings circuit-break + replan, braid heals locally). Cross-chain contracts: joint budgets, joint termination (no stranded handoffs), provenance D7, versioning via contract registry (kills B6 schema races), cross-ring deadlock = staleness timeout + LLMDR layer + breaker, deterministic replay per-ring ledger. Status: proposed v1, to validate in phase 5 reference impls.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T06:57:37.796680+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a07fe04be50c05", "ts": "2026-09-08T07:16:41.061636+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["malic", "phase5", "harness", "reference-implementation", "braid", "validation"], "priority": "normal", "content": "MALIC Phase 5 (reference implementations) — STANDALONE BRAID HARNESS COMPLETE + VERIFIED 2026-09-08. Canonical package /root/notebooks/research/malic_harness/ (braid.py core + run.py CLI, pure stdlib). It validates phase-3 envelope and phase-4 braid wiring with real running code. MODEL: 4 rings A3-style loops over task streams; members m1(a,c) m2(b,d) m3(a,b) m4(c,d) = the intersections; every attempt precomputed deterministically pre-run (same task stream/thresholds both runs) = clean single-RNG A/B where only in-ring knowledge differs. ENVELOPE LIVE: token budget + iteration cap, monotone no-progress self-stop (A3), heartbeat staleness -> zombie kill draining dead-letter (B7/D2/D3), LoopID telemetry every stop (D7), every queue item accounted (never silent). mem20 ledger = content-hash registry, sole dedupe authority. BRAID PROTOCOL: at each stop executing member presents pending diff set to its other rings (crossing + rendezvous tick); receiving ring gates via anti-echo (seen-set dedupe, hop_max=5, energy drop 0.5/hop) then adopts into ring playbook; adopted lessons re-carried at half energy (multi-hop). VALIDATION seed=7 canonical: braid 54 failures vs control 60 (delta 6), skills 90 vs 79 (+11); ring_d stalled-zombie at same stop 50 in BOTH runs yet braided ring_d cut failures 11->7 via 14 cross-origin lessons = direct proof one ring's failure teaches another same iteration; anti-echo live: 795 dedupe hits, 24 unique lessons in registry (echo crushed); integrity all stops logged + queue fully accounted both runs. 5-seed sweep (1,2,3,42,1337): braid wins every time (delta 5-12 failures, skills always higher, dedupe 790-969). Notebook cells 11-12 (12 cells total), live-kernel verified all 6 code cells ok (run-all CLI times out waiting but kernel executes; verified cell-by-cell). Artifact /root/notebooks/research/malic_harness_report.json. NEXT: phase 5 wiring = apply proven braid + envelope to AGS-OS / fleetwide_mem20 workers (user approved \"both, harness first\").", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T07:16:41.061636+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
