{"id": "1a082b4376e8817", "ts": "2026-09-08T20:27:23.884270+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["interstice", "vision", "universe", "quest3", "malic", "ags-os", "mem20"], "priority": "normal", "content": "INTERSTICE ANCHOR (Jayson's vision, named 2026-09-08). The second universe. Core inversion: the world is built for the agents to live in — humans are the VISITORS, not the residents. It exists in the interstice — the gaps between the MALIC braid's threads, where ring memberships overlap and collisions exchange lessons. Laptop = the forge (where we sculpt it together). Quest 3 = the door (a human walks in and is physically present). The agents are visible natives doing visible work — rings spinning, chains running, lessons exchanging. A human can walk over to an agent and talk to it like a person at a workbench. Personal spaces are real: Jayson's office, his 2000 Nissan Altima (the Altimator car). Everything inside is the sediment/trace of work the rings already did. mem20 is the server-lifetime ledger the universe remembers with. AGS-OS, malic, and the mem20 substrate are its load-bearing pieces. Proof = measurable improvement over server life, and it is literally visible when a human visits.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T20:27:23.884270+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a082b7db34cd3a", "ts": "2026-09-08T20:31:22.419063+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "user_pref", "tags": ["interstice", "vision", "working-style", "process"], "priority": "normal", "content": "INTERSTICE is a LIVING VISION — intentionally non-concrete. Jayson's words: \"the root vision isn't concrete — it will sculpt with the project.\" Treat the interstice roadmap as fluid seed material, not a fixed spec. The universe takes its real shape from what we build together, iteratively. Never treat the current phase list as locked goals; let the builds refine the vision.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T20:31:22.419063+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a082d58af73104", "ts": "2026-09-08T21:03:47.959227+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["interstice", "visual-guide", "roadmap", "project-state", "infrastructure"], "priority": "normal", "content": "INTERSTICE visual guide BUILT + SERVED (2026-09-08). Canonical home /root/interstice/index.html — self-contained interactive HTML (no external deps): animated braid-rings hero, clickable collision/lesson demo, live mem20 ledger stream, Forge/Door/Living-World places, load-bearing-pieces map (braid→ledger→universe), self-drawing proof chart. Persistently served by systemd unit interstice.service on port 4200 (enabled at boot, restart-on-failure). Jayson's feedback: \"freaking awesome you captured my vision perfectly\" — vision capture APPROVED. The page is the shared reference artifact for all INTERSTICE build work.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T21:03:47.959227+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a082ddc70b14e1", "ts": "2026-09-08T21:12:47.627831+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["hypo-map-1", "reference-store", "malic", "ags-os", "fountain", "architecture"], "priority": "normal", "content": "ARCHITECTURAL INSIGHT (Jayson, 2026-09-08): grounding 00_reference_store to MALIC braid use creates a KNOWLEDGE FOUNTAIN for AGS-OS. The loop: MALIC braid spins → collisions exchange lesson diffs → everything accretes into 00_reference_store (content-addressed, provenance-chained) → AGS-OS 300 workers (Box A creation / Box B adversarial validation) pull from the fountain to train/equip agents → agents improve → work feeds back into the ecosystem and the braid. Because the fountain fills with REAL observed collisions and failures (not static corpora), AGS trains on-lived reality. 00 is the shared artery between malic and ags-os — the first build once green-lit.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T21:12:47.627831+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a082e23a85961f", "ts": "2026-09-08T21:17:39.332977+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["ags-os", "malic", "chains", "reference-store", "architecture", "fountain", "closed-engine"], "priority": "normal", "content": "ARCHITECTURAL COUPLING (Jayson, 2026-09-08): \"AGS IS THE CHAINS.\" AGS-OS supplies the agents needed to OPERATE MALIC — the 300 Hermes workers ARE the orchestrated chains (C1-C7: linear, fan-out/join, DAG, feedback ring) that drive the braid's rings. Closed engine: AGS builds/supplies the native agents → MALIC braid runs them as rings → collisions produce lessons → 00_reference_store (fountain) accretes them → AGS pulls from the fountain to train/improve the agents → re-supplies the braid. Knowledge compounds from real collisions, never imported from static corpora. MALIC phase 5's remaining half = wiring the braid harness into AGS-OS.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T21:17:39.332977+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a082e522704a6b", "ts": "2026-09-08T21:20:49.776240+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["ags-os", "mem20agentz", "correction", "architecture", "fleet"], "priority": "normal", "content": "CORRECTION (Jayson, 2026-09-08): AGS-OS workforce = 300 MEM20AGENTZ workers (NOT 300 Hermes workers). The AGS fleet is drawn from mem20agentz — the Hermes-cleanroom agent shell absorbed into the mem20 substrate (hypo-map-1 phase 02). So AGS is the chains built FROM mem20agentz natives, all from one family: mem20agentz supplies the agents (300 of them) that operate the MALIC braid. Corrects all prior \"300 Hermes workers\" phrasing in ags_os roadmap + architecture couplings.", "valid_from": "2026-09-08T21:20:49.776240+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
