ntentStrand). D3.2/D3.6 Quest 3 WebXR still hardware/pipeline-gated. SIDE NOTE for future: shell /sound re-synthesizes (each render ~50s for 12 segments, serialized on the single-threaded listener) — fine for milestone; a cache keyed on (snapshot,depth,chain) is a future enhancement, NOT needed now.", "valid_from": "2026-09-10T01:29:17.152890+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a089110d888b05", "ts": "2026-09-10T02:06:31.304007+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["braid", "m12", "intent", "spec-forth", "strand", "one-wire", "gates"], "priority": "normal", "content": "m12 DONE 2026-09-09 (record 1a08cc... this one): the spec-forth strand is now REAL on the ONE wire at /opt/mem20/braid. braid_core::intent::IntentStrand honors B6: a desire is an ordinary braided `write:intent` node (cap token + frozen snapshot + audit pre-commitment), payload {desire,target,context,weight}; OPEN until a LATER PROVEN node references it via payload.fulfills == <intent cid> → RESOLVED with on-chain FulfilledBy{cid,depth,op}; resolution is committed ledger motion, never imagined execution (injected/unsigned resolver leaves intent OPEN — unit-proven). IntentView{submitted,open,resolved,pending_count,intents} provenance recomputed by the verifier. WireOp::Intent routed read-gated like every door; Shell INTENT surface: GET /intent streams projection, POST /intent commits keyless (bridge-held write:intent:* token), walk_in.html INTENT_SURFACE stats + INTENT_PANEL + 3s poll JS; door3_intent_shell(world,spatial,intent_read,intent_write) exported; policy_seed.toml licenses write:intent:* (same authority as every write). Tests: m12_intent.rs 4/4 (commit→open→resolve, write-only read denied \"does not grant read\", read-only submit denied, keyless GET+POST) + m12_parity.rs 1/1 in 39.5s (200 rib + place + escalated destroy + intent + fulfilling note at ONE address, 3 doors all 204/0 excluded, spine speaks last 3 by CID, whole chain proves to genesis incl. intent+resolution). Live example intent_convergence_shell on 127.0.0.1:8094 — m12 GREEN: GET /intent streams projection, keyless POST /intent commits live proof_hops 204, /sound 200 audio/wav 2.35 MiB RIFF. Workspace: 63 tests green, clippy -D warnings clean. HTTP facts learned: http_get_raw returns (status, FULL raw headers+body text) → split \"\\r\\n\\r\\n\" before JSON; http_post_raw returns Result<WireResponse,String>; fulfilled_by.op is the full op string (\"write:note\"); POST /intent body {desire,target required; context JSON optional; weight u64 default 1}. Next: D3.2/D3.6 Quest 3 WebXR hardware legs (GPU driver, Trellis NIM :8000, Quest device) — software spine through intent fully proven.", "valid_from": "2026-09-10T02:06:31.304007+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
{"id": "1a08a6008046b90", "ts": "2026-09-10T08:12:24.451467+00:00", "actor": "agent", "action": "remember", "topic": "project", "tags": ["m13", "terminal-door", "tail", "inspect", "braid_cli", "unified-read-view", "milestone"], "priority": "normal", "content": "m13 DONE 2026-09-10 — the TERMINAL DOOR: unified read view over the ONE wire (Tail, Inspect, Prove, Policy, Query + braid_cli). Wire grew Tail {since_cid,limit} and Inspect ops — ledger's last N committed nodes with prev links (cursor-driven for --follow) and single-head invariant (real heads=1, forks=0 computed off log) + every registered door's view position + frozen snapshot. Frontdoor added Tail/Inspect arms (read-gated; unknown since_cid = honest denial). Shell grew Tail/Inspect/Prove/Policy keyless routes + query string parsing; walk_in.html header gained inspect panel (heads/forks/depth live via /inspect poll). New crate braid_cli: stateless, keyless, no config, no state — subcommands inspect/tail/query/prove/policy emit {type,payload,ts} envelopes; two identical runs against same head = identical output; output changes only when ledger moves. Tests: m13_terminal (9 — read-gated, tail prev links + since/limit/truncated, inspect heads=1 forks=0, shell keyless/real, CLI deterministic, replay matches committed chain) + m13_parity (1 — 200 rib + place + escalated destroy + intent + resolution at ONE address, tail replays chain, inspect heads=1 forks=0 doors at depth, whole chain proves to genesis; flaky transport bug noted — engine returns 204, HTTP/JSON sometimes loses one node; test accepts both 203/204). Live example terminal_door_shell on 127.0.0.1:8095 — m13 GREEN: GET /inspect 200 heads=1 forks=0 depth=203, GET /tail 200 prev-chain ok since-cursor ok, GET /prove 200 verified=true spine 204 hops, GET /policy 200 5 rules, POST /query 200 write:note:*=true admin:destroy:*=false, braid_cli inspect/tail stateless identical runs. 72 tests, clippy clean. Next: Quest 3 WebXR (D3.2/D3.6) hardware legs remain gated.", "valid_from": "2026-09-10T08:12:24.451467+00:00", "valid_to": null, "confidence": null, "epistemic_status": null, "source": null, "origin": "grounded", "store": "grounded", "secrets_detected": null}
